.TH "PB-DAEMON" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-daemon - Paperboat endpoint daemon


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb daemon [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Paperboat endpoint daemon

.PP
Run the daemon under supervision or manage the privileged machine guard. Most users should use pb service to install, start, stop, and inspect the background process. In a Linux container without systemd, pb daemon --foreground is the container's main command: it enrolls the machine on its first start from PAPERBOAT_ENROLLMENT_CREDENTIAL (a token from pb machine add), keeps the enrollment in the state volume so a restart needs no token, runs the Paperboat service as an unprivileged runtime user and stops cleanly on SIGTERM.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--config\fP=""
	configuration file

.PP
\fB--foreground\fP[=false]
	run the Paperboat service in the foreground as a container's main command (Linux)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for daemon

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	Paperboat server URL


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-daemon-machine-guard(1)\fP, \fBpb-daemon-run(1)\fP
